# {{ project_name }}

Local Postgres database + read-only dashboard for tracking {{ entity_plural }}.
Generated by the `tracker-setup` skill.

## Start it

```
./start.sh
```

The first run creates the database and installs what the dashboard needs;
after that it just starts. Open **http://localhost:{{ port }}/** if it doesn't
open on its own. The dashboard reads live from Postgres, so there is nothing
to rebuild.

## Working with Claude

Open Claude Code in this folder (`claude`). `CLAUDE.md` tells it how this
tracker works; on the first run it walks you through setup. After that, tell it
what happened in plain words and it updates the database for you.

## Day-to-day updates

Report events in chat (new contact, stage change{% if has_value %}, {{ value_label | lower }} info{% endif %}, notes)
and Claude Code runs the corresponding SQL directly against `{{ db_name }}`,
e.g.:

```sql
UPDATE {{ entity_plural }} SET current_stage = '...' WHERE {{ primary_field }} = '...';
```

The `trg_log_stage_change` trigger automatically appends to `stage_history`
whenever `current_stage` changes, so history is never updated manually.

To add a brand-new {{ entity_singular }}:

```sql
INSERT INTO {{ entity_plural }} ({{ primary_field }}, {{ secondary_field }}, source_type, date_first_contact, current_stage{% if has_value %}, {{ value_field_prefix }}_text{% endif %}, location, source_link)
VALUES ('...', '...', '{{ source_type_options[0] }}', CURRENT_DATE, {{ baseline_stage | sqlstr }}{% if has_value %}, '...'{% endif %}, '...', 'https://...');
```

Importing an existing spreadsheet: ask Claude Code to write a one-off
import script for your file — spreadsheet columns vary too much to ship a
generic importer.

