## Scout agent (finds candidates, never submits)

Run the `{{ entity_singular }}-scout-agent` skill to search your target
sources (see `{{ config_dir_name }}/search_terms.md`) and stage new matches
as `{{ queued_stage }}` rows, each tagged an A/B match tier{% if artifact_enabled %} and — for
candidates that need one — a draft {{ artifact_label | lower }} written to a real
file on disk{% endif %}. It never submits anything or

creates accounts; review queued candidates at
**http://localhost:{{ port }}/queue.html**, open the source, act on it
yourself, then click **{{ baseline_stage }}** (moves it to `{{ baseline_stage }}`)
or **Dismiss** (moves it to `{{ closed_stages[0] }}`).{% if artifact_enabled %} A candidate
without one can be flagged with **Request {{ artifact_label }}** — the
scout agent drafts it on its next run (or sooner, if you ask directly).{% endif %}

Before the first run, fill in `{{ config_dir_name }}/criteria.md`{% if artifact_enabled %} and add
your background as `{{ config_dir_name }}/profile.md`{% endif %}.


**Budget, so token spend doesn't run away:** each run stops early once it
finds {{ scout_candidates_target }} A-tier candidates and hard-caps at
{{ scout_candidates_cap }} total; it checks every enabled source ({{ scout_sources | join(', ') }}) each run{% if 'web' in scout_sources %},
covering {{ scout_terms_per_run }} web-search terms per run (rotating through the rest on later runs unless set to "all"){% endif %}; and overflow beyond the cap is drafted and
held in `{{ config_dir_name }}/overflow_backlog.jsonl` to drain on the next
run instead of being wasted or silently dropped. Each run logs its stats to
the `scout_runs` table so you can compare volume/cap-hit frequency over
time. Full rules are in
`.claude/skills/{{ entity_singular }}-scout-agent/SKILL.md`.
{% endif %}
